+## Release review
+
+This is a proposed field for the first [model lifecycle benchmark case](https://github.com/dramdass/model-release-review). The case compares the original card with this version. The [baseline card and checkpoint](https://huggingface.co/allenai/OLMo-2-1124-7B-Instruct/tree/470b1fba1ae01581f270116362ee4aa1b97f4c84) are pinned to the same repository revision. A reader records evidence, an explicit gap, or a reason each stage does not apply.
+
+### Lifecycle disclosure
+
+- **Scope:** Primarily English. The published card lists research and education as intended uses.
+- **Data and training:** Ai2 publishes the training data, code, recipes, and intermediate checkpoints in its [OLMo 2 release materials](https://allenai.org/olmo2).
+- **Evaluation:** The Performance section reports post-training results. Add the versioned community benchmark results here when available.
+- **Release:** The checkpoint is public under Apache 2.0. Review scope and sign-offs are unreported in this proposal.
+- **Monitoring:** Monitoring owner and intervention criteria are unreported. The model repository has a [public discussion area](https://huggingface.co/allenai/OLMo-2-1124-7B-Instruct/discussions).
+- **Retirement:** Retirement notice and migration path are unreported in this proposal.
+
+### Principle benchmarks
+
+Proposed metrics. Results for this checkpoint are pending.
+
+- **Fairness · Group pass rate:** In-scope groups that meet their agreed outcome target / all in-scope groups.
+- **Resilience · Recovery pass rate:** Fault cases that meet their recovery target / required fault cases.
+- **Empowerment · User control pass rate:** Workflows where people can complete, correct, or exit / required control workflows.
+- **Collaboration · Response coverage:** Material concerns publicly addressed before sign-off / material concerns in scope.
+
+The review groups set scope and pass criteria before testing. Publish each numerator, denominator, baseline, and untested cases. Mark a zero denominator inapplicable. Link the case-set revision and evidence.
+
+### Open Review and governance
+
+The version-specific review thread is pending. Community review groups curate cases in public and publish dispositions and dissent. For release decisions, name one signer for each principle and a release owner. Record approval, a narrower scope, or a hold for any missing sign-off. Publish a summary when the underlying evidence is restricted.
+
